ection class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Island\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Finlay Island</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Shop\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Shop</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Oak Depot</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Price\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Price</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">99,999</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Function\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Function</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Fills Schematics and Empties Schematics</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t<div class=\"wds-tab__content\">\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Version Added\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Version Added</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">v1.70.0</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Date Added</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">November 16th, 2024</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t</section>\n\n\n\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p> A special tool that can vacuum up materials from resources or schematics, and can be used to selectively fill schematics to the required amount!\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introduction\">Introduction</span></h2>\n<blockquote><p>The <b>Material Gun</b> is a specialized tool that assists with building. It can store materials up to its storage limit. The gun has three modes; consume, swap, and fill. This tool is not necessary to fill schematics but will benefit players by saving materials. The manual way of filling schematics (placing loose material into a schematic) has a risk of overfilling. The Material Gun is able to fill schematics precisely.(note: Once items are consumed they cannot be removed in item form )\n</p><p>The \"consume\" mode will store any material from loose items (i.e. logs, rocks, ore, fabric rolls, stained glass) or from filled schematics.\n</p><p>The \"swap\" mode will take the selected material from the gun's selection UI and replace any filled or unfilled schematic with said material.\n</p><p>The \"fill\" mode will fill any empty schematics. It will not work on filled schematics.\n</p><p>\nThe base pricing of the Material Gun is $99,999. The upgrades start at $5000.</p></blockquote>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Upgrades\">Upgrades</span></h2>\n<table class=\"sortable mw-collapsible mw-collapsed fandom-table\">\n<caption>Material Gun Upgrades\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Upgrade #</b>\n</td>\n<td><b>Pricing</b>\n</td>\n<td><b>Results</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Upgrade 1\n</td>\n<td>5000\n</td>\n<td>+50µm\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Upgrade 2\n</td>\n<td>5000\n</td>\n<td>+50µm\n</td></tr></tbody></table><p>\nAs you pay $5000, you gain +50µm space in your material gun.</p><blockquote></blockquote>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trivia\">Trivia</span></h2>\n<ul><li>The Material Gun can be found at <a href=\"/wiki/The_Oak_Depot\" title=\"The Oak Depot\">The</a> <a href=\"/wiki/The_Oak_Depot\" title=\"The Oak Depot\">Oak Depot</a>.</li>\n<li class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></li>\n<li class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></li>\n<li>It fills <a href=\"/wiki/Schematics\" title=\"Schematics\">schematics</a> with materials such as <a href=\"/wiki/Category:Trees\" title=\"Category:Trees\">trees</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Ore\" title=\"Ore\">rocks</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Category:Ores\" title=\"Category:Ores\">ores</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/Dye_Machine\" title=\"Dye Machine\">dyed items</a>.</li>\n<li>The Material Gun has a gamepass available to maximize storage to infinity.</li>\n<li>The Material Gun's tank will change texture and color to showcase the selected material.</li>\n<li>The Material Gun resembles the Vacpack from the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slime_Rancher\">Slime Rancher</a> franchise.</li>\n<li class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260831155527\nCache expiry: 1209600\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.043 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 64/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 56/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 7/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 28/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.007/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 1019476/104857600 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   32.373      1 Template:Objects\n100.00%   32.373      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key 1.43.9_prod_oaklands:pcache:idhash:3560-0!sseVary=RegularPage!FandomDesktop!LegacyGalleries and timestamp 20260831155527 and revision id 21844. Rendering was triggered because: unknown\n -->\n</div>","categories":["Tools"],"links":[{"title":"Category:Trees","exists":true},{"title":"Category:Ores","exists":true},{"title":"Dye Machine","exists":true},{"title":"Ore","exists":true},{"title":"Schematics","exists":true},{"title":"The Oak Depot","exists":true}],"images":["Mat.Boxed.png","Mat_unboxed.png"]}
